\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Finite-set forms and scalar inner fluctuations}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{Dimakis and Müller-Hoissen formulate connection and curvature
in a differential calculus on a finite set. Their preprint gives
the formulas in \citet{§§3.1–3.2, pp. 6–7}{dimakis1994finite}.
The present
[based-cell differential](fdip-00SH) instead retains labeled
loops and parallel cellular edges. Its curvature formula is
proved by the two path products in \ref{fdip-00SL}; a reduction
of a finite-set calculus to this cellular model would require
an explicit identification of the retained forms and paths.}

\p{The scalar inner fluctuation in \ref{fdip-0096} has edge coefficient
#{1+c_e}. When that coefficient is nonzero over the stated
field, it can be compared with an invertible scalar link after
fixing source and head conventions. A zero coefficient is not a
group transport. Nor does a scalar coefficient construct the
arbitrary non-Abelian representation used here. The covariance
and product identities above follow directly from the declared
coefficient action.}
